      "anchor": "<plan>#s109",
      "id": "done_when-1",
      "reason": "a worker dispatched days later runs the control at whatever head it receives, so a peer's landed change can make the control green at \"base\" and destroy the only evidence that its guard fires.",
      "text": "the negative control at plan.html:923 says only \"at the base revision\", so no revision is fixed for the run that must show the second project's row delivered, while s103-s108 each pin theirs as \"main after <sha>\"",
      "type": "done_when",
      "would_change": true
    },
    {
      "anchor": "<plan>#s110",
      "id": "done_when-2",
      "reason": "the launch-failed branch already offers two sub-remedies (recovery_classification.py:3112-3125), so which revision the base arm used is the whole content of the control.",
      "text": "the negative control at plan.html:930 says only \"at the base revision\", leaving the tree the base arm must use unpinned",
      "type": "done_when",
      "would_change": true
    },
    {
      "anchor": "<plan>#s109",
