  "rubric_items": {
    "anchors_resolve": "pass \u2014 both cited test paths are new files, and both sections cite no existing file or section; the s110 example run's directory no longer exists on disk (consistent with it having been discarded), so the mechanism was verified in code instead: the launch-failed branch at reckon/crew/recovery_classification.py:3080-3120 names a resume remedy.",
    "done_when": "a finding \u2014 both new sections name \"the base revision\" without pinning it, unlike every sibling section (s103\u2013s108 each name \"main after <sha>\").",
    "evidence_paths": "a finding \u2014 neither new section states where its arm logs live or requires the EXIT= line that every sibling section requires, so the gates named here have no durable evidence path.",
    "naming": "pass \u2014 the two new test filenames (test_a_pane_follows_only_projects_with_its_work.py, test_a_launch_failed_run_is_told_to_discard.py) carry no section number, ticket or version tag, and neither section names a symbol or file to modify.",
    "reasoning": "a finding \u2014 s109's \"38 hours\" of delivered rows does not hold against the plan's own dates; the stated root cause and the reachability check otherwise pass on all three counts.",
    "single_goal": "pass \u2014 s109's three cases all measure one property (a pane's project set follows the session's own work), and s110's remedy-plus-cause text is one obligation rewrite measurable on one run shape.",
    "wiring": "pass \u2014 the dependency this review's unit s108 has is declared and unchanged (s108 waits on s107, per plan-section-depends-on); s109 and s110 declare no dependency and need none, writing the follower subscription and the launch-failed obligation, neither of which consumes an unlanded section's output."
  },
